            <div xml:id="d534">

                <pb facs="0404" n="400" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg400"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.115/383: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Third Secretary of Embassy in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Allison</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-09T18:00:00+08:00">July 9, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 9—4:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>132. Shanghai’s 893, June 24, 10 a.m. L. J. Mead of Standard Vacuum Oil Company,
                    and T. F. Shields of Texas Company, both American citizens, arrived in Nanking
                    together this afternoon on the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Oahu</hi>. These
                    are the first American businessmen who have returned to Nanking since its
                    occupation by the Japanese.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Hankow, Peiping and Shanghai. Peiping please repeat to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Allison</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
